@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] smtp-upstream-verified
The maintained patch MUST require authenticated TLS with certificate and hostname
verification before sending credentials or mail. Credential values and upstream
response text MUST NOT enter logs, tracing, arguments or build outputs.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] smtp-synchronous-bounded
Forwarding MUST have a three-second connection deadline and eight-second total
deadline and close its upstream connection on cancellation or timeout. Success
MUST follow upstream DATA acceptance; no queue, persistent payload or internal
retry may replace Marshall's encrypted outbox authority. Maintain and run the
patched package's tests whenever changing the transport patch.
